    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-10T19:06:16Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr787Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #779 (parse-throughput investigation) noted that the Gene Ontology and Wikidata performance tests in tests/performance.rs have never actually run anywhere, because they're #[ignore]'d and the only hardware previously available locally (a 3.7GB-RAM Hetzner box shared with production, per #559) couldn't handle them. Dag timed the gene_ontology_full_pipeline test on two of his own machines in release mode (~25s on a ThinkPad, ~2s on a recent Mac) and asked to re-enable it in CI, as a release-mode job, plus asked whether checking in the Gene Ontology data itself would be legal or if there's a safer way to fetch it. Checked GO's actual license (searched it rather than assuming): CC BY 4.0, not CC0 as might be guessed -- redistribution is legally fine with attribution, but go.owl is ~130MB, a poor fit for git history versus a stable download. The real problem with the existing download script wasn't legality but reproducibility: it pointed at current.geneontology.org's rolling \"current\" snapshot, whose own versionIRI was observed changing mid-investigation (2026-06-19 -> 2026-07-26 between two checks), and -- a sharper finding -- a freshly-stamped versionIRI isn't necessarily archived yet under release.geneontology.org (2026-07-26 404s there; verified via curl across several candidate dates that 2026-06-19 is the latest one actually present, with a correct Content-Length for a full go.owl)." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:787 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr787Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr787 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr787Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Pinned download_test_ontologies.sh's GO_OWL_XML_URL to the dated, verified-live release.geneontology.org/2026-06-19/ontology/go.owl rather than current.geneontology.org/ontology/go.owl, with a comment telling future maintainers to curl -I the candidate date before bumping it (not just copy the versionIRI) since that's exactly the trap found during verification. Added a gene-ontology-tests CI job mirroring the existing imf-tests job structure (separate job, so a slow download doesn't block the core suite): installs a pinned Apache Jena 5.1.0 via actions/setup-java + a direct archive.apache.org tarball fetch (no apt package exists for Jena on Ubuntu), converts go.owl to Turtle with riot --output=TURTLE (same invocation the script already documented, just newly exercised), then runs cargo test --test performance --release gene_ontology -- --ignored --nocapture. Did not vendor go.owl/go.ttl into the repo." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered using the generic http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/go.owl or .../go/releases/<date>/go.owl PURLs directly in CI instead of the resolved release.geneontology.org URL -- rejected only as the primary CI URL (an extra redirect hop adds a cloudflare dependency with no benefit once the final URL is already verified-stable), though the script's comments still point maintainers at the PURL form for verifying a new date, since it's the more citable/canonical form." .
